WEBVTT

00:32:29.520 --> 00:32:34.316
like, "What is the most meaningful
thing that happened to you this week?"

00:32:34.340 --> 00:32:37.259
Jessica: I feel bad that I stressed
Bess out with my question.

00:32:37.283 --> 00:32:38.520
Bess: Oh! Don't feel bad!

00:32:38.544 --> 00:32:40.686
That's, like, a personal problem. (Laughs)

00:32:40.710 --> 00:32:43.981
Jessica: Yeah, but I think that's
really interesting and illustrative

00:32:44.005 --> 00:32:46.614
because you don't know
what things will trip someone up

00:32:46.638 --> 00:32:49.701
when you're making what strikes
one person as casual conversation

00:32:49.725 --> 00:32:52.246
can be like a nerve
that another person has

00:32:52.270 --> 00:32:54.081
that's raw that you don't know about.

00:32:54.105 --> 00:32:55.927
AG: Jessica and Bess's exchange shows

00:32:55.951 --> 00:32:58.516
that a connection doesn't always
form automatically.

00:32:58.540 --> 00:33:01.124
But when they debriefed about it,
the dynamic changed.